ce text.\n\n**Recommendations**  \n- **Immediate actions**:  \n  1. Contact your nearest Krishi Vigyan Kendra (KVK) to learn about any upcoming VKSA workshops or farmer‑scientist interaction sessions.  \n  2. Register for any VKSA‑related events announced by the Karnataka Department of Agriculture.\n\n- **Monitoring advice**:  \n  1. Keep an eye on announcements from the Karnataka State Agriculture Department and local KVKs for future VKSA windows (the programme runs twice a year).  \n  2. Follow local agricultural bulletins or SMS alerts that often share VKSA schedules and topics.\n\n- **When to seek expert help**:  \n  1. If you need personalized advice on soil health, crop‑specific practices, or input recommendations that are discussed during VKSA sessions, schedule a visit to your KVK agronomist or extension officer.", "claims": ["supported: VKSA was an explicit part of the campaign in Karnataka", "supported: The state launch was held on 8 June 2025 at ICAR‑IIHR, Bengaluru", "supported: The VKSA programme has indeed been introduced and operated in Karnataka", "supported: The programme runs twice a year"], "unsupported": [], "final_answer": "**Observation**  \n- The knowledge text states that Viksit Krishi Sankalp Abhiyan (VKSA) was an explicit part of the campaign in Karnataka, with the state launch held on **8 June 2025** at ICAR‑IIHR, Bengaluru.\n\n**Analysis**  \n- This indicates that the VKSA programme has indeed been introduced and operated in Karnataka.\n\n**Confidence**  \n- **High** – the information is directly provided in the reference text.\n\n**Recommendations**  \n- **Immediate actions**:  \n  1. Contact your nearest Krishi Vigyan Kendra (KVK) to learn about any upcoming VKSA workshops or farmer‑scientist interaction sessions.  \n  2. Register for any VKSA‑related events announced by the Karnataka Department of Agriculture.\n\n- **Monitoring advice**:  \n  1. Keep an eye on announcements from the Karnataka State Agriculture Department and local KVKs